  <STRG>
    <!-- String description / descriptions list -->
    <Section Index="0" Format="inline">
      <String>Classic LabVIEW state machine in the NI canonical form (as exported from examples/Design Patterns/State Machine/State Machine Fundamentals.vi): an inline enum type uint16{Init,Load,Accumulate,Report,Stop} carries the state through a shift register; a Case Structure inside a While loop selects the frame by that state; each frame computes the next state (a constant, or a Select between two state constants when the transition is conditional) and writes every data register through a per-frame case Out tunnel, which is the per-state multiplexer for the register value. The Stop frame is the only one that raises the stop flag through a conditional (cond=true) tunnel wired straight to the loop condition. States: Init resets the registers; Load takes the next item from Items; Accumulate adds it to the sum, advances the index and branches back to Load or on to Report by comparing the index against the item count; Report divides sum by count into the average; Stop ends the loop. Every visited state is appended to a transition Log string register. Initial State accepts any state item so the machine can start mid-sequence.</String>
      </Section>
    </STRG>
